(4814479, 692453, 66384, '<td valign="top">I really like the concept of a rural mailbox in a rural landscape. I think I would like the image better if the mailbox was off center more, and maybe a bit smaller. As I look at the image, I feel a little frustrated that I can''t see more of background scene.</td>', 'I really like the concept of a rural mailbox in a rural landscape. I think I would like the image better if the mailbox was off center more, and maybe a bit smaller. As I look at the image, I feel a little frustrated that I can''t see more of background scene.', '2008-07-09 11:31:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4814505, 692179, 6519, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote on this challenge, and you sure have a fascinating photo there!<br/> <br/>However, you had a problem with people who didn''t consider this "rural", so allow me to quote from Wikipedia to help you understand why those voters might have felt that way:<br/> <br/>Quote: "Rural areas (also referred to as "the country," and/or "the countryside") are settled places outside towns and cities. Such areas are distinct from more intensively settled urban and suburban areas, and also from unsettled lands such as the outback, American Old West or wilderness. Inhabitants live in villages, hamlets, on farms and in other isolated houses."</td>', 'I didn''t vote on this challenge, and you sure have a fascinating photo there! However, you had a problem with people who didn''t consider this "rural", so allow me to quote from Wikipedia to help you understand why those voters might have felt that way: Quote: "Rural areas (also referred to as "the country," and/or "the countryside") are settled places outside towns and cities. Such areas are distinct from more intensively settled urban and suburban areas, and also from unsettled lands such as the outback, American Old West or wilderness. Inhabitants live in villages, hamlets, on farms and in other isolated houses."', '2008-07-09 11:44:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4814519, 693738, 91890, '<td valign="top">I am sorry for my previous comments..being an Asian Indian i agree to ur PM..White people hunted/chased away tonnes of aboriginals from America to Australia..<br/>NICE JOB..<br/>Saturation still a Issue :) :)<br/>I appreciate your Work..<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-07-09 10:52:12.</i></td>', 'I am sorry for my previous comments..being an Asian Indian i agree to ur PM..White people hunted/chased away tonnes of aboriginals from America to Australia..NICE JOB..Saturation still a Issue :) :)I appreciate your Work..', '2008-07-09 11:50:30.000000', '2008-07-09 11:52:12.000000', 0),
(4814595, 692473, 67697, '<td valign="top">Love that misty morning.  Beautiful scene - so peaceful looking.  Congrats on the ribbon!</td>', 'Love that misty morning.  Beautiful scene - so peaceful looking.  Congrats on the ribbon!', '2008-07-09 12:18:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4814603, 694208, 30982, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=410590" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30982/120/410590.gif'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30982/120/410590.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30982/120/410590.gif"/></a> <br/> <br/>Here''s your ribbon - display it proudly!<br/> <br/>And funny that Peter thinks it''s too soft - I think there''s too much sharpening near the tree/sky border.  I think most landscapes unless richly colored suffer from the 640 pixel size.  The other comment I''d offer is that the straight line/centered comp is somewhat static.  All that said, I really love the foreground field.  I''ve been trying to get good field shots for some time.  A lovely classic of such is zeuszen''s entry in the free study.</td>', '  Here''s your ribbon - display it proudly! And funny that Peter thinks it''s too soft - I think there''s too much sharpening near the tree/sky border.  I think most landscapes unless richly colored suffer from the 640 pixel size.  The other comment I''d offer is that the straight line/centered comp is somewhat static.  All that said, I really love the foreground field.  I''ve been trying to get good field shots for some time.  A lovely classic of such is zeuszen''s entry in the free study.', '2008-07-09 12:25:12.000000', NULL, 0),
