(4834706, 694339, 67697, '<td valign="top">This reminds me of a painting I''ve seen before.  I love the symmetry you''ve created with the diagonally sloping trees and their reflections.   It''s a beautiful scene with great lighting and I''m glad it scored well!</td>', 'This reminds me of a painting I''ve seen before.  I love the symmetry you''ve created with the diagonally sloping trees and their reflections.   It''s a beautiful scene with great lighting and I''m glad it scored well!', '2008-07-20 01:31:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4835675, 694096, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Sue,<br/>      A nice image, I really like your placement of the barn here. The color balance in the sky is also nicely done. The foreground seems to be a bit busy &amp; was a bit of a distraction.</td>', 'Hi Sue,      A nice image, I really like your placement of the barn here. The color balance in the sky is also nicely done. The foreground seems to be a bit busy & was a bit of a distraction.', '2008-07-20 21:14:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4838886, 694258, 65858, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by booboo_goon:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hotpasta:</b></div><hr/><i> great tones...8 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You always seem to be the first one to comment on my pics Enzo!! Hhahahahahaha thanks alot! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>That should be encouraging - Enzo''s the man!  =)<br/> <br/>Indeed, the tones are lovely.</td>', 'Originally posted by booboo_goon: Originally posted by hotpasta: great tones...8   You always seem to be the first one to comment on my pics Enzo!! Hhahahahahaha thanks alot!  That should be encouraging - Enzo''s the man!  =) Indeed, the tones are lovely.', '2008-07-22 17:58:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4845433, 694337, 41337, '<td valign="top">The thing I love about your photography is you always hint at a story. You never give out too many details and you always require the viewer to immerse themselves into the image before anything of substance can be obtained. This photo in particular shows a field that could exist at any point in time. When I look long enough I start to feel the subtle breeze that acts as an invitation. The portrait composition keeps my view restricted so I begin to wonder what''s around the corner. It almosts feels like a door... so I pause. then that cloud in the distance perks my interest and has me wondering what''s over in the distance and so I step in and the door slams behind me. Bland composition? I don''t think so.</td>', 'The thing I love about your photography is you always hint at a story. You never give out too many details and you always require the viewer to immerse themselves into the image before anything of substance can be obtained. This photo in particular shows a field that could exist at any point in time. When I look long enough I start to feel the subtle breeze that acts as an invitation. The portrait composition keeps my view restricted so I begin to wonder what''s around the corner. It almosts feels like a door... so I pause. then that cloud in the distance perks my interest and has me wondering what''s over in the distance and so I step in and the door slams behind me. Bland composition? I don''t think so.', '2008-07-26 04:38:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4849849, 692640, 73452, '<td valign="top">i really like this photo, the sky is amazing, really striking.  changing an original color photo into black/white really opens tons of new doors for your imagination.  tones are all there, mid, higher and lower, all in nice detail.  actually im kinda suprised this didnt fair better, its a great photo, keep it up!</td>', 'i really like this photo, the sky is amazing, really striking.  changing an original color photo into black/white really opens tons of new doors for your imagination.  tones are all there, mid, higher and lower, all in nice detail.  actually im kinda suprised this didnt fair better, its a great photo, keep it up!', '2008-07-29 19:28:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4849856, 692640, 41337, '<td valign="top">I get the sense of weight and gravity when I look at this. The lines in the photograph appear to be effected (pulled towards and inward) near the point of the hay cloest to the camera. This composition is what makes the photo, IMO. The black and white conversion is good. You mentioned the sky and I agree it''s wonderful. Very good shot.</td>', 'I get the sense of weight and gravity when I look at this. The lines in the photograph appear to be effected (pulled towards and inward) near the point of the hay cloest to the camera. This composition is what makes the photo, IMO. The black and white conversion is good. You mentioned the sky and I agree it''s wonderful. Very good shot.', '2008-07-29 19:33:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4850051, 692640, 92643, '<td valign="top">there definitely are some nice leading lines here...i also like that while the other fields are crowded with hay bales, this one is all alone! great detail in the foreground and background</td>', 'there definitely are some nice leading lines here...i also like that while the other fields are crowded with hay bales, this one is all alone! great detail in the foreground and background', '2008-07-29 21:26:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4854546, 693929, 23613, '<td valign="top">WOW! What a photo. I noticed you took the photo on June 30. I took a photo from the same spot on July 3, except the tree was on my right side. My photo turned out beautiful too. I was TOTALLY surprised my Sony DCS-P72 took such a great photo. I wish I could post it here for you to look at.</td>', 'WOW! What a photo. I noticed you took the photo on June 30. I took a photo from the same spot on July 3, except the tree was on my right side. My photo turned out beautiful too. I was TOTALLY surprised my Sony DCS-P72 took such a great photo. I wish I could post it here for you to look at.', '2008-08-01 01:49:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4860635, 691892, 88523, '<td valign="top">I quite like this. I like the placement of the woman and the layers of colour. Could be a bit sharper and perhaps the colours a bit deeper, but still, I think it''s a good pic!</td>', 'I quite like this. I like the placement of the woman and the layers of colour. Could be a bit sharper and perhaps the colours a bit deeper, but still, I think it''s a good pic!', '2008-08-03 04:14:48.000000', NULL, 0),
